# ==========================================
# NextGenAI - Environment Variables
# ==========================================

# ==========================================
# ADMIN AUTHENTICATION (REQUIRED)
# ==========================================
ADMIN_EMAILS=your-email@gmail.com,another-admin@example.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=YourSecurePassword123!
JWT_SECRET=your-very-long-random-secret-key-minimum-32-characters

# ==========================================
# AI PROVIDERS (Minimal 1 Required)
# ==========================================

# Groq (FREE - 32K tokens) - https://console.groq.com
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Google AI Studio (FREE - 2M tokens!) - https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey
GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIzaSyxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# OpenRouter (PAID - Access to GPT-4, Claude) - https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ==========================================
# MULTIPLE MONGODB DATABASES (Optional)
# ==========================================
# Create multiple MongoDB Atlas accounts for unlimited free storage
# Each account gets 512MB free tier

# MongoDB Account 1
MONGODB_URI_1=mongodb+srv://user1:pass1@cluster1.xxxxx.mongodb.net/
MONGODB_DB_1=nextgenai
MONGODB_NAME_1=MongoDB Primary

# MongoDB Account 2
MONGODB_URI_2=mongodb+srv://user2:pass2@cluster2.xxxxx.mongodb.net/
MONGODB_DB_2=nextgenai
MONGODB_NAME_2=MongoDB Backup 1

# MongoDB Account 3
MONGODB_URI_3=mongodb+srv://user3:pass3@cluster3.xxxxx.mongodb.net/
MONGODB_DB_3=nextgenai
MONGODB_NAME_3=MongoDB Backup 2

# Add more as needed (up to MONGODB_URI_10)
# MONGODB_URI_4=mongodb+srv://user4:pass4@cluster4.xxxxx.mongodb.net/
# MONGODB_DB_4=nextgenai
# MONGODB_NAME_4=MongoDB Backup 3

# MONGODB_URI_5=mongodb+srv://user5:pass5@cluster5.xxxxx.mongodb.net/
# MONGODB_DB_5=nextgenai
# MONGODB_NAME_5=MongoDB Backup 4

# ==========================================
# MULTIPLE SUPABASE DATABASES (Optional)
# ==========================================
# Create multiple Supabase projects for extra storage
# Each project gets 500MB free tier

# Supabase Project 1
SUPABASE_URL_1=https://xxxxx.supabase.co
SUPABASE_KEY_1=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
SUPABASE_NAME_1=Supabase Primary

# Supabase Project 2
SUPABASE_URL_2=https://yyyyy.supabase.co
SUPABASE_KEY_2=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
SUPABASE_NAME_2=Supabase Backup

# Add more as needed (up to SUPABASE_URL_5)
# SUPABASE_URL_3=https://zzzzz.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_KEY_3=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
# SUPABASE_NAME_3=Supabase Backup 2

# ==========================================
# VERCEL KV (Optional - 256MB Free)
# ==========================================
# Auto-configured by Vercel when you add KV database
# No manual setup needed - just create via Vercel Dashboard
KV_REST_API_URL=https://xxxxx.kv.vercel-storage.com
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ==========================================
# DEPLOYMENT
# ==========================================
VERCEL_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app
NODE_ENV=production

# ==========================================
# HOW TO GET API KEYS
# ==========================================

# 1. GROQ (Recommended - FREE)
#    - Visit: https://console.groq.com
#    - Sign up with Google/GitHub
#    - Go to "API Keys" → "Create API Key"
#    - Copy the key starting with "gsk_"
#    - Paste above as GROQ_API_KEY

# 2. GOOGLE AI STUDIO (FREE - 2M tokens!)
#    - Visit: https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey
#    - Sign in with Google account
#    - Click "Create API Key"
#    - Copy the key starting with "AIzaSy"
#    - Paste above as GOOGLE_API_KEY

# 3. OPENROUTER (Optional - Paid)
#    - Visit: https://openrouter.ai/keys
#    - Sign up and add payment method
#    - Create API key
#    - Copy key starting with "sk-or-v1-"
#    - Paste above as OPENROUTER_API_KEY

# ==========================================
# HOW TO SETUP MONGODB
# ==========================================

# Method 1: Single Account (512MB free)
# 1. Visit: https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas/register
# 2. Sign up with email: yourname@gmail.com
# 3. Create free M0 cluster (any region)
# 4. Database Access → Add User (username + password)
# 5. Network Access → Add IP → Allow from anywhere (0.0.0.0/0)
# 6. Database → Connect → Drivers → Copy connection string
# 7. Replace <password> with your password
# 8. Add to MONGODB_URI_1

# Method 2: Multiple Accounts (Gmail trick for unlimited storage)
# Use Gmail aliases to create multiple accounts:
# - yourname+mongo1@gmail.com → 512MB
# - yourname+mongo2@gmail.com → 512MB
# - yourname+mongo3@gmail.com → 512MB
# Total: 1.5GB free storage!
#
# All emails go to same inbox (yourname@gmail.com)
# but MongoDB sees them as different accounts!

# ==========================================
# HOW TO SETUP SUPABASE
# ==========================================

# 1. Visit: https://supabase.com/dashboard
# 2. Sign up with GitHub/Email
# 3. Create new project (choose any region)
# 4. Wait for database to be created (~2 minutes)
# 5. Go to Settings → API
# 6. Copy "Project URL" → Paste to SUPABASE_URL_1
# 7. Copy "anon public" key → Paste to SUPABASE_KEY_1

# For multiple projects:
# - Use different emails (Gmail trick works here too!)
# - yourname+supabase1@gmail.com → 500MB
# - yourname+supabase2@gmail.com → 500MB

# ==========================================
# TOTAL FREE STORAGE CAPACITY
# ==========================================
# 10 MongoDB accounts × 512MB = 5,120 MB (5.1 GB)
# 5 Supabase accounts × 500MB = 2,500 MB (2.5 GB)
# 1 Vercel KV × 256MB = 256 MB
# ─────────────────────────────────────────
# TOTAL = 7,876 MB = 7.8 GB FREE!
# ==========================================

# ==========================================
# SECURITY BEST PRACTICES
# ==========================================

# 1. ADMIN_PASSWORD
#    - Use strong password (12+ characters)
#    - Mix uppercase, lowercase, numbers, symbols
#    - Don't use common words
#    - Example: MySecure#Pass2024!

# 2. JWT_SECRET
#    - Minimum 32 characters
#    - Use random string generator
#    - Example: use this command to generate:
#    node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"

# 3. API Keys
#    - Never commit .env file to git
#    - Add .env to .gitignore
#    - Use environment variables in production
#    - Rotate keys periodically

# 4. Database Access
#    - MongoDB: Use strong passwords
#    - Change default database name
#    - Enable IP whitelist in production
#    - Supabase: Enable RLS (Row Level Security)

# ==========================================
# DEPLOYMENT NOTES
# ==========================================

# Local Development:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in your actual keys
# 3. Run: npm run dev

# Vercel Deployment:
# 1. Don't commit .env to git
# 2. Add variables in Vercel Dashboard:
#    Settings → Environment Variables
# 3. Add to all environments: Production, Preview, Development
# 4. Redeploy after adding variables

# Vercel KV Setup:
# 1. Vercel Dashboard → Storage tab
# 2. Create Database → Choose KV
# 3. Connect to your project
# 4. Variables auto-added (KV_REST_API_URL, KV_REST_API_TOKEN)

# ==========================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ==========================================

# "Authentication failed"
# → Check ADMIN_EMAILS matches your login email exactly
# → Check JWT_SECRET is at least 32 characters

# "No AI providers configured"
# → Add at least GROQ_API_KEY or GOOGLE_API_KEY
# → Verify key is valid at provider website

# "Database connection failed"
# → MongoDB: Check connection string format
# → MongoDB: Verify Network Access allows 0.0.0.0/0
# → Supabase: Check URL and key are correct

# "Module not found"
# → Run: npm install
# → Check package.json has all dependencies

# ==========================================
# QUICK START (Minimum Setup)
# ==========================================

# For basic functionality, you only need:
# 1. ADMIN_EMAILS (your email)
# 2. ADMIN_PASSWORD (secure password)
# 3. JWT_SECRET (32+ random characters)
# 4. GROQ_API_KEY (free from console.groq.com)

# Everything else is optional!
# Add databases later for learning features.

